    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2509.17177v3</id>
    <title>FlagEval Findings Report: A Preliminary Evaluation of Large Reasoning Models on Automatically Verifiable Textual and Visual Questions</title>
    <updated>2025-11-25T17:49:27Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.17177v3" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.17177v3" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We conduct a moderate-scale contamination-free (to some extent) evaluation of current large reasoning models (LRMs) with some preliminary findings. We also release ROME, our evaluation benchmark for vision language models intended to test reasoning from visual clues. We attach links to the benchmark, evaluation data, and other updates on this website: https://flageval-baai.github.io/LRM-Eval/</summary>
